From f1c33d7a09a8dbd25797c4c4436234e164165fd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Hommey <mh+mozilla@glandium.org>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 08:48:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 2061033 - Avoid std::all_of in
 nsAtom::ComputeIsAsciiLowercase. r=xpcom-reviewers,emilio

gGkAtoms evaluates ComputeIsAsciiLowercase and HashString for all 2715 static
atoms within a single constant expression, which leaves it close to the default
-fconstexpr-steps budget of 1048576 on every platform.

libc++ 22 made std::all_of noticeably more expensive to evaluate: for this
workload it went from ~227600 to ~343300 steps, about 1.5x. That was enough to
push the total over the limit on the mingw builds, which are the only ones using
the libc++ that comes with the clang toolchain. Other platforms don't use it:
linux uses libstdc++, mac uses the libc++ from the SDK, and windows uses the
MSVC STL.

Steps required to evaluate the gGkAtoms initializer, before and after
this change:

                                before      after
    mingw clang 21 (libc++)     957616     729979
    mingw clang 22 (libc++)    1073241     729979   <- over the 1048576 limit
    linux clang 21 (libstdc++)  939550     729979
    linux clang 22 (libstdc++)  939550     729979

Spelling out the loop takes the standard library out of the picture entirely:
all four combinations now need the same 729979 steps, a little under 70% of the
budget, so this no longer depends on which standard library the target happens
to use.

Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316723
---
 xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h b/xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h
index 0faa453cfc0c3..16afc3ea7b69b 100644
--- a/xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h
+++ b/xpcom/ds/nsAtom.h
@@ -36,11 +36,19 @@ class nsDynamicAtom;
 class nsAtom {
  public:
   // Returns true if ToLowercaseASCII would return the string unchanged.
+  //
+  // This is deliberately a plain loop rather than std::all_of: gGkAtoms calls
+  // this for every static atom within a single constant expression, and
+  // std::all_of costs enough extra constexpr steps to exceed the default
+  // -fconstexpr-steps budget with some standard library implementations.
   static constexpr bool ComputeIsAsciiLowercase(const char16_t* aString,
                                                 const uint32_t aLength) {
-    return std::all_of(aString, aString + aLength, [](char16_t c) {
-      return !mozilla::IsAsciiUppercaseAlpha(c);
-    });
+    for (uint32_t i = 0; i < aLength; ++i) {
+      if (mozilla::IsAsciiUppercaseAlpha(aString[i])) {
+        return false;
+      }
+    }
+    return true;
   }
 
   template <size_t N>
